# TEMPLATE ONLY for /opt/beebase/config/gateway.env - gateway's own
# production configuration. Never loaded by deploy.sh, Docker Compose,
# or the app directly (see docker-compose.prod.yml's env_file: entry for
# the `gateway` service, which reads the REAL file this template
# produces). Provision once on the EC2 host:
#   cp deploy/env-templates/gateway.env.example /opt/beebase/config/gateway.env
#   chmod 600 /opt/beebase/config/gateway.env
#
# gateway holds no secret of its own today - every variable it needs
# (APP_ENV, LOG_LEVEL, HTTP_PORT, GOMEMLIMIT, every *_SERVICE_URL) is
# non-secret network topology supplied by docker-compose.prod.yml's
# `environment:` block instead (see requirement 11 in the deployment
# report: topology stays compose-owned, not duplicated into a service's
# .env "just for convenience"). This file still has to exist - and be
# mode 0600 - because docker-compose.prod.yml's env_file: entry for
# gateway requires it, and because deploy.sh validates every one of the
# 7 services' files before it will touch the running stack, keeping the
# architecture uniform for the day gateway does need one.
